{{!
    @template local_dimensions/progress_card_body

    Progress body of a course card: the lock overlay when the course is locked, the state pill
    when it is open, then the shape the server chose (cardmode): one activity, one section with
    its ring, or the section timeline.

    The overlay keeps its frame (the dashed border the card script draws, the 80px disc, the raised
    message box, the 10px-radius buttons over the blurred timeline) and holds the shared state area
    of the course cards: the disc in the state's colour family and icon, the pill in the message
    box, the state's own action, then the route line and, for a card with nothing else to say,
    the day its enrolment opens or else the course start date.

    Context variables required:
    * courseid (int) - Course ID, used to pair the collapse toggle with its timeline
    * enabled (bool) - Whether completion tracking is enabled
    * iscompleted (bool) - Whether the course itself is complete, from the batch status call
    * locked (bool) - Whether the course is locked for the user
    * state (object) - The state area, from the course progress service: key, label, icon, family,
      actionlabel, actionurl, routelabel, routelinklabel, routeurl, opens, openslabel (texts plain,
      empty when absent; openslabel names the day the enrolment window refusing a none card opens)
    * formatted_start_date (string) - The course start date a card in the none state shows, empty
      when it names no date (no date chip then)
    * islearnmore (bool) - Client-derived: learn-more mode on a card in the none state, so the
      "Learn more" button replaces the message box
    * showlockeddate (bool) - Client-derived: show the start date of a card in the none state
    * customicon (string) - CSS class of the admin's icon for a card in the none state (empty = the
      state's own icon)
    * hascontinue (bool) - Whether a section is under way, so the Continue shortcut renders
    * continueurl (string) - URL of the section the learner left off at
    * continuename (string) - Name of that section, for the accessible label
    * courseurl (string) - URL to the course page (for "Learn More" button), empty for a course the viewer may not be told about
      (the message box then)
    * learnmorebuttoncolor (string) - Hex color for the "Learn More" button background
    * cardmode (string) - Which shape the card takes: "activity", "section" or "timeline"
    * activity (object) - The single trackable activity {cmid, name, url, completed,
      tracked}, present only when cardmode is "activity"
    * section (object) - The course's one section {name, hasownname, url, tracked},
      present only when cardmode is "section"
    * istimeline (bool) - Client-derived: cardmode is "timeline", so the section sequence
      renders
    * sectionpercentage (int) - Client-derived: the one section's own percentage, shown by
      the section body's ring
    * sectiondasharray (string) - Client-derived: that percentage as an arc length on the
      shared r=12 ring, so the section body and the timeline draw the same geometry
    * sections (array) - Array of section objects with progress data, drawn by the timeline

    @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courseid": 42,
        "enabled": true,
        "iscompleted": false,
        "locked": true,
        "state": {
            "key": "pending",
            "label": "Application under review",
            "icon": "fa-hourglass-half",
            "family": "local-dimensions-state-pending",
            "actionlabel": "View status",
            "actionurl": "/enrol/index.php?id=42",
            "routelabel": "You can also enrol now",
            "routelinklabel": "Enrol now",
            "routeurl": "/enrol/index.php?id=42",
            "opens": 0,
            "openslabel": ""
        },
        "formatted_start_date": "01/02/2026",
        "hascontinue": false,
        "continueurl": "",
        "continuename": "",
        "islearnmore": false,
        "showlockeddate": false,
        "customicon": "",
        "courseurl": "/course/view.php?id=42",
        "cardmode": "timeline",
        "activity": false,
        "section": false,
        "istimeline": true,
        "sectionpercentage": 0,
        "sectiondasharray": "0.00",
        "sections": [
            {
                "name": "Section 1",
                "percentage": 100,
                "has_activities": true,
                "url": "",
                "is_completed": true,
                "is_started": false,
                "locked": false
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div style="position: relative; height: 100%;">
    {{#locked}}
    <div class="local-dimensions-locked-overlay" data-state="{{state.key}}">
        {{! The disc: the state's colour family and icon, or the admin's icon on a card that
            offers nothing }}
        <div class="local-dimensions-locked-icon {{state.family}}">
            {{#customicon}}
                <i class="{{customicon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{/customicon}}
            {{^customicon}}
                <i class="fa {{state.icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{/customicon}}
        </div>
        {{! Learn-more mode puts its button in place of the message box, on a card that offers
            nothing; a card with no course URL (a course the viewer may not be told about) has
            nowhere to send it and keeps the message box }}
        {{#islearnmore}}
            {{#courseurl}}
                <a href="{{courseurl}}" class="local-dimensions-learnmore-btn" style="background: {{learnmorebuttoncolor}};">{{#str}}learn_more, local_dimensions{{/str}}</a>
            {{/courseurl}}
            {{^courseurl}}
                <div class="local-dimensions-locked-message"><span class="local-dimensions-state-pill {{state.family}}"><span>{{state.label}}</span></span></div>
            {{/courseurl}}
        {{/islearnmore}}
        {{^islearnmore}}
            <div class="local-dimensions-locked-message"><span class="local-dimensions-state-pill {{state.family}}"><span>{{state.label}}</span></span></div>
        {{/islearnmore}}
        {{#state.actionurl}}
            <a href="{{state.actionurl}}" class="local-dimensions-enrol-btn">{{state.actionlabel}}</a>
        {{/state.actionurl}}
        {{! The route line: another way in beside a relationship, under the action }}
        {{#state.routeurl}}
            <div class="local-dimensions-state-route"><i class="fa fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>{{state.routelabel}}</span> <a href="{{state.routeurl}}">{{state.routelinklabel}}</a></div>
        {{/state.routeurl}}
        {{! The day the enrolment window opens, whatever showlockeddate says: the service sends it
            only on a none card, and then withdraws the course start date below }}
        {{#state.openslabel}}
            <div class="local-dimensions-locked-date" data-region="enrolment-opens">
                <i class="fa fa-calendar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{state.openslabel}}
            </div>
        {{/state.openslabel}}
        {{! The course start date, under the pill of a card with nothing else to say, never an empty
            chip when the row names no date }}
        {{#showlockeddate}}
            {{#formatted_start_date}}
                <div class="local-dimensions-locked-date">
                    <i class="fa fa-calendar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{#str}}available_at, local_dimensions, {{formatted_start_date}}{{/str}}
                </div>
            {{/formatted_start_date}}
        {{/showlockeddate}}
    </div>
    {{/locked}}

    {{! An open card shows no state pill: being enrolled is the ordinary case and says nothing }}

    {{! A course that resolves to one trackable activity has no sequence to draw. The card
        shows that activity and its own state instead - the server decides when this applies,
        and the activity shape is the one that survives completion tracking being off. }}
    {{#activity}}
    <div class="local-dimensions-single">
        {{! An untracked activity leaves nothing to mark, so the span itself is dropped
            rather than left empty - an empty span still reserves its flex gap. }}
        {{#tracked}}
        <span class="local-dimensions-single-mark">
            {{#completed}}
                <span class="local-dimensions-icon local-dimensions-icon-check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {{/completed}}
            {{^completed}}
                <span class="local-dimensions-icon local-dimensions-icon-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {{/completed}}
        </span>
        {{/tracked}}
        <span class="local-dimensions-single-name">{{name}}</span>
        {{#tracked}}
        <span class="local-dimensions-single-status {{#completed}}local-dimensions-single-done{{/completed}}">
            {{#completed}}{{#str}}course_completed, local_dimensions{{/str}}{{/completed}}
            {{^completed}}{{#str}}filter_not_completed, local_dimensions{{/str}}{{/completed}}
        </span>
        {{/tracked}}
        {{#url}}
        <a href="{{url}}" class="local-dimensions-single-go">
            {{#str}}go_to_activity, local_dimensions{{/str}}<i class="fa fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
        {{/url}}
    </div>
    {{/activity}}

    {{^activity}}
    {{! The lock overlay already explains why there is nothing to see, and it covers this
        text visually - so only announce it when the card is not locked. }}
    {{^enabled}}
        {{^locked}}
        <div class="p-3 text-muted text-center small">
            {{#str}}completion_disabled, local_dimensions{{/str}}
        </div>
        {{/locked}}
    {{/enabled}}

    {{! The disabled message above and the two bodies below are alternatives: with tracking off
        there is no percentage or sequence to show. The activity body sits outside this guard
        on purpose, so a single untracked activity is still named and linked. }}
    {{#enabled}}
    {{! One visible section holding several activities: a timeline of a single row naming a
        section usually called "General" would inform nobody, so the card offers a way in
        instead. }}
    {{#section}}
    <div class="local-dimensions-single-section">
        {{! No ring for a section with nothing trackable: a 0% would mislead (the timeline shows
            its info icon for the same case). The name and call to action render either way. }}
        {{! The timeline's own ring, scaled up by CSS so the arc geometry and dasharray factor
            stay shared. Reusing the ring container also applies the percentage display mode
            (fixed / hover / hidden) with no rule of its own; under hidden the arc still shows
            progress. }}
        {{#tracked}}
        <div class="local-dimensions-progress-ring-container local-dimensions-progress-ring-lg"
             role="progressbar"
             aria-valuenow="{{sectionpercentage}}"
             aria-valuemin="0"
             aria-valuemax="100"
             aria-label="{{#str}}aria_completion_percentage, local_dimensions, {{sectionpercentage}}{{/str}}">
            <svg class="local-dimensions-progress-ring" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle class="local-dimensions-progress-ring__bg" cx="16" cy="16" r="12" />
                <circle class="local-dimensions-progress-ring__progress" cx="16" cy="16" r="12"
                    style="stroke-dasharray: {{sectiondasharray}} 75.4; stroke-dashoffset: 0;" />
            </svg>
            {{! Bare number, like the timeline's own ring: "100%" would not clear the arc, and the
                accessible label above already carries the unit. }}
            <span class="local-dimensions-progress-text" aria-hidden="true">{{sectionpercentage}}</span>
        </div>
        {{/tracked}}
        {{#hasownname}}
        <span class="local-dimensions-single-section-name">{{name}}</span>
        {{/hasownname}}
        {{#url}}
        <a href="{{url}}" class="local-dimensions-single-go">
            {{#str}}access_content, local_dimensions{{/str}}<i class="fa fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
        {{/url}}
    </div>
    {{/section}}

    {{#istimeline}}
    {{! A finished course earns a seal and folds its section list away: every row would say
        the same thing, and the card's job here is to confirm, not to enumerate. }}
    {{#iscompleted}}
    {{^locked}}
    <div class="local-dimensions-course-seal">
        <i class="fa fa-check-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{#str}}course_completed, local_dimensions{{/str}}
    </div>
    <button type="button"
            class="local-dimensions-timeline-toggle"
            data-timeline-toggle
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="local-dimensions-timeline-{{courseid}}">
        <span>{{#str}}sections_all_complete, local_dimensions{{/str}}</span>
        <i class="fa fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
    {{/locked}}
    {{/iscompleted}}
    <div class="local-dimensions-timeline"
         id="local-dimensions-timeline-{{courseid}}"
         {{#iscompleted}}{{^locked}}hidden{{/locked}}{{/iscompleted}}>
        {{#sections}}
        <div class="local-dimensions-timeline-item {{#is_completed}}completed{{/is_completed}} {{#is_started}}started{{/is_started}} {{#locked}}locked{{/locked}}">
            <div class="local-dimensions-timeline-marker">
                {{! Priority order: locked > is_completed > is_started > empty/info }}
                {{#locked}}
                    <span class="local-dimensions-icon local-dimensions-icon-lock-sm" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                {{/locked}}

                {{^locked}}
                    {{#is_completed}}
                        <span class="local-dimensions-icon local-dimensions-icon-check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    {{/is_completed}}

                    {{^is_completed}}
                        {{#is_started}}
                             <div class="local-dimensions-progress-ring-container" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="{{percentage}}" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-label="{{#str}}aria_completion_percentage, local_dimensions, {{percentage}}{{/str}}">
                                <svg class="local-dimensions-progress-ring" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true">
                                   <circle class="local-dimensions-progress-ring__bg" cx="16" cy="16" r="12" />
                                   <circle class="local-dimensions-progress-ring__progress" cx="16" cy="16" r="12"
                                   style="stroke-dasharray: {{dasharray}} 75.4; stroke-dashoffset: 0;" />
                                </svg>
                                <span class="local-dimensions-progress-text" aria-hidden="true">{{percentage}}</span>
                            </div>
                        {{/is_started}}

                        {{^is_started}}
                            {{#has_activities}}
                                <span class="local-dimensions-icon local-dimensions-icon-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            {{/has_activities}}
                            {{^has_activities}}
                                <span class="local-dimensions-icon local-dimensions-icon-info" aria-hidden="true" title="{{#str}}no_completion_tracking, local_dimensions{{/str}}"></span>
                            {{/has_activities}}
                        {{/is_started}}
                    {{/is_completed}}
                {{/locked}}
            </div>

            <div class="local-dimensions-timeline-content">
                {{#locked}}
                    {{#url}}
                        <a href="{{url}}" class="text-muted" aria-label="{{#str}}view_section, local_dimensions, {{name}}{{/str}}">{{name}}</a>
                    {{/url}}
                    {{^url}}
                        <span class="text-muted">{{name}}</span>
                    {{/url}}
                {{/locked}}

                {{^locked}}
                    {{#url}}
                    <a href="{{url}}" aria-label="{{#str}}view_section, local_dimensions, {{name}}{{/str}}">{{name}}</a>
                    {{/url}}
                    {{^url}}
                    <span>{{name}}</span>
                    {{/url}}
                {{/locked}}
            </div>
        </div>
        {{/sections}}
    </div>
    {{! A quiet way back to where the learner left off. Absent on a locked card, and absent
        once every section is done, because there is then nothing to continue. }}
    {{#hascontinue}}
    {{^locked}}
    <a href="{{continueurl}}" class="local-dimensions-continue" aria-label="{{#str}}continue_to, local_dimensions, {{continuename}}{{/str}}">
        <i class="fa fa-play-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{#str}}continue_label, local_dimensions{{/str}}
    </a>
    {{/locked}}
    {{/hascontinue}}
    {{/istimeline}}
    {{/enabled}}
    {{/activity}}

    {{#error}}
     <div class="alert alert-danger m-2">{{error}}</div>
    {{/error}}
</div>
